{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:warped-product","title":"def:warped-product","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":482,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:warped-product","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:product-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:smooth-tensor-field-add]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:smooth-tensor-field-smul]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:warped-product","line":800,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Warped Products]\n\\label{def:warped-product}\n\n\\uses{def:product-metric, def:riemannian-metric, lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite, lem:smooth-tensor-field-add, lem:smooth-tensor-field-smul}\n\n\n\n\nFor Riemannian manifolds $(M_1,g_1)$ and $(M_2,g_2)$ and a strictly positive smooth $f:M_1\\to\\mathbb R^+$, the \\emph{warped product} $M_1\\times_fM_2$ is $M_1\\times M_2$ with metric $g_1\\oplus f^2g_2$. It is smooth because\n\\[\ng_1\\oplus f^2g_2=\\pi_1^*g_1+(f\\circ\\pi_1)^2\\pi_2^*g_2,\n\\]\nusing Lemmas \\ref{lem:smooth-tensor-field-smul} and \\ref{lem:smooth-tensor-field-add}; positivity is Lemma \\ref{lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite}. Since only $f^2$ occurs, a nowhere-vanishing smooth real $f$ also suffices.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Warped Products] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7761727065642d70726f64756374\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aproduct-metric\">↗ def:product-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Awarped-product-form-positive-definite\">↗ lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asmooth-tensor-field-add\">↗ lem:smooth-tensor-field-add</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asmooth-tensor-field-smul\">↗ lem:smooth-tensor-field-smul</a> <p></p>For Riemannian manifolds <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M_1,g_1)$\">$(M_1,g_1)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M_2,g_2)$\">$(M_2,g_2)$</span> and a strictly positive smooth <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f:M_1\\to \\mathbb R^+$\">$f:M_1\\to \\mathbb R^+$</span>, the <em>warped product</em> <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M_1\\times _fM_2$\">$M_1\\times _fM_2$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M_1\\times M_2$\">$M_1\\times M_2$</span> with metric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_1\\oplus f^2g_2$\">$g_1\\oplus f^2g_2$</span>. It is smooth because <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  g_1\\oplus f^2g_2=\\pi _1^*g_1+(f\\circ \\pi _1)^2\\pi _2^*g_2,  \\]\">\\[  g_1\\oplus f^2g_2=\\pi _1^*g_1+(f\\circ \\pi _1)^2\\pi _2^*g_2,  \\]</span> using Lemmas <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asmooth-tensor-field-smul\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:smooth-tensor-field-smul\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a736d6f6f74682d74656e736f722d6669656c642d736d756c\">2</a> and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asmooth-tensor-field-add\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:smooth-tensor-field-add\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a736d6f6f74682d74656e736f722d6669656c642d616464\">2</a>; positivity is Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Awarped-product-form-positive-definite\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7761727065642d70726f647563742d666f726d2d706f7369746976652d646566696e697465\">3</a>. Since only <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f^2$\">$f^2$</span> occurs, a nowhere-vanishing smooth real <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span> also suffices. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:warped-product-constant-one","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:product-metric","title":"def:product-metric","label":"def:product-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","label":"def:riemannian-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite","title":"lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite","label":"lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:smooth-tensor-field-add","title":"lem:smooth-tensor-field-add","label":"lem:smooth-tensor-field-add"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:smooth-tensor-field-smul","title":"lem:smooth-tensor-field-smul","label":"lem:smooth-tensor-field-smul"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:warped-product-constant-one","title":"prop:warped-product-constant-one","label":"prop:warped-product-constant-one"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:warped-products","title":"ex:warped-products","label":"ex:warped-products"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:riemannian-submersions","title":"ex:riemannian-submersions","label":"ex:riemannian-submersions"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:polar-map","title":"def:polar-map","label":"def:polar-map"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:warped-product","title":"def:warped-product","tex":"\\begin{definition}[Warped Products]\n\\label{def:warped-product}\n\n\\uses{def:product-metric, def:riemannian-metric, lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite, lem:smooth-tensor-field-add, lem:smooth-tensor-field-smul}\n\n\n\n\nFor Riemannian manifolds $(M_1,g_1)$ and $(M_2,g_2)$ and a strictly positive smooth $f:M_1\\to\\mathbb R^+$, the \\emph{warped product} $M_1\\times_fM_2$ is $M_1\\times M_2$ with metric $g_1\\oplus f^2g_2$. It is smooth because\n\\[\ng_1\\oplus f^2g_2=\\pi_1^*g_1+(f\\circ\\pi_1)^2\\pi_2^*g_2,\n\\]\nusing Lemmas \\ref{lem:smooth-tensor-field-smul} and \\ref{lem:smooth-tensor-field-add}; positivity is Lemma \\ref{lem:warped-product-form-positive-definite}. Since only $f^2$ occurs, a nowhere-vanishing smooth real $f$ also suffices.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blu